e, overall proportions, and object positions.\n\nChange only the rendering style, linework, shading, colors, and surface texture. Minor local detail variations required for the illustrated anime appearance are allowed.\n\nUse refined two- or three-step anime cel shading with one coherent directional key light. Add clear form shadows that describe the subject’s volume, slightly deeper contact and occlusion shadows where parts overlap or connect, and restrained highlights on light-facing planes and curved surfaces. Keep the lighting clean and illustrative, with crisp shadow shapes and only limited soft transitions on broad rounded forms. Highlights and shadows must remain confined to the subject and preserve the original local colors. Create stronger three-dimensional form without turning the image into a photorealistic or 3D-rendered scene.\n\nKeep the background uniformly pure black (#000000), flat and completely featureless, with no scenery, floor, gradient, glow, reflection, cast shadow, texture, particles, or additional elements.\n\nDo not add, remove, duplicate, or replace objects. Do not change the pose, perspective, camera angle, crop, zoom, rotation, or subject placement. Do not transform the subject into an existing anime character. Avoid photorealistic lighting, 3D-rendered materials, excessive gloss, broad blown-out highlights, heavy rim lighting, overly dark shadows, and any glow or cast shadow on the black background. Do not add text, logos, borders, or watermarks.\n",822444379945758],"widgets_values_named":{"unet_name":"flux-2-klein-4b.safetensors","clip_name":"qwen_3_4b.safetensors","vae_name":"flux2-vae.safetensors","text":"Transform the input image into a clean, modern Japanese anime illustration style.\n\nPreserve the same subject identity, object count, pose, camera viewpoint, perspective, composition, silhouette, overall proportions, and object positions.\n\nChange only the rendering style, linework, shading, colors, and surface texture. Minor local detail variations required for the illustrated anime appearance are allowed.\n\nUse refined two- or three-step anime cel shading with one coherent directional key light. Add clear form shadows that describe the subject’s volume, slightly deeper contact and occlusion shadows where parts overlap or connect, and restrained highlights on light-facing planes and curved surfaces. Keep the lighting clean and illustrative, with crisp shadow shapes and only limited soft transitions on broad rounded forms. Highlights and shadows must remain confined to the subject and preserve the original local colors. Create stronger three-dimensional form without turning the image into a photorealistic or 3D-rendered scene.\n\nKeep the background uniformly pure black (#000000), flat and completely featureless, with no scenery, floor, gradient, glow, reflection, cast shadow, texture, particles, or additional elements.\n\nDo not add, remove, duplicate, or replace objects. Do not change the pose, perspective, camera angle, crop, zoom, rotation, or subject placement. Do not transform the subject into an existing anime character. Avoid photorealistic lighting, 3D-rendered materials, excessive gloss, broad blown-out highlights, heavy rim lighting, overly dark shadows, and any glow or cast shadow on the black background. Do not add text, logos, borders, or watermarks.\n","noise_seed":822444379945758}},{"id":521,"type":"LoadImageDataSetFromFolder","pos":[-1709.7692382139035,1046.70925331274],"size":[270,58],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"文件夹","name":"folder","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"folder"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"图像","name":"images","shape":6,"type":"IMAGE","links":[7802]}],"properties":{"cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.33.2","Node name for S&R":"LoadImageDataSetFromFolder","ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"input_ue_unconnectable":{},"version":"7.8"}},"widgets_values":["ffhq/images1024x1024"],"widgets_values_named":{"folder":"ff